                              INTRODUCTION:
                              
                              
    Well one day after searching all the local CNET BBS's I could
 find, and then Digging through every Archive I could think of in the 
 Internet, I came to the conclusion that if I wanted a program to check
 to see if it was a users Birthday at Log-on, I would have to write it
 myself!

     Thus, This is a Little AREXX program that checks each users Birthday
 against the current system date.  If it is the users birthday a few
 things are set in motion:
 
            -  The user is greeted during log-on with a Happy
               Birthday MCI screen.
               
            -  There current WHO Banner is examined and saved to disk
               for use later.
               
            -  The users who banner is changed to read:
               "Its My Birthday Today!!!!"
               
     Now the Next time the same user calls a few more things are
  dealt with.
  
             - Check to see if user has a WHO banner stored on 
               the harddrive
               
             - if so it will check to see if it is still the users
               birthday (Calling Twice in one day Maybe?)
                
             - If it is no longer the users Birthday it will
               Load the WHO banner that has been saved on
               disk and restore it back to normal.
               
             - Finally the temporary who banner is removed from
               the harddrive (Just to keep things neat and tidy)
               
                          
                           INSTALLATION:
                              

Don't you hate Pfiles that take 3 days to install in 1,523 DIFFERENT
Directories???  Well I Made this one as Easy as possible.

OK, heres the installation instructions for Birthdays:

First edit your Sys.welcome text located in the systext directory of
CNET,  add the following line to the end of it.

                      #0pfiles:birthdays/Birthday}
                      ^
                      |
        (This First Character is a Control Q of course)


Next make a directory in your Pfiles directory called Birthdays.

Now copy the Main program "Birthday" into the directory ya just created
in pfiles called Birthdays.

Thats all there is to it! Have fun and enjoy the Program!

TESTING the Program:

     Now if any of you Sysop's out there would like to test and see 
that the Pfile if functioning, Simply change your birthday under EU
(Edit user prefs) to the current date.  Now relog (Or if loggin on 
for the first time, Make sure to hit the Space-bar to log on and not
the Tab key or it will obviously skip the Sys.welcome file)) and
you will see the happy Birthday screen..and when ya get to the main
menu type who to see if the Banner changed.  Now simply change your
birthday back to what it should be, and relog once more...Notice
the Birthday Greeting is gone and now your WHO banner has been restored.!!

         Now think about this:

   This may be a small and kinda' simple program, but think of the
fun your users are gonna have with it!  They will be happy know that
you, as a Sysop, have taken the time to tell them Happy Birthday!
secondly just Imagine their surprise when they do a WHO and see
their banner has given em' away! This program DOES NOT reveal the users
age in any way so I really do not anticipate ANY user getting upset
at your running this program!  So PLEASE think about registering this
prog..After all it will be used EVERY time someone calls your BBS! :)
